From d3ea82ad2ba31249a9552efd00881167994aa155 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vuln Patch Pipeline <vuln-patch@chainguard.dev>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:12:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Refuse unsigned JWTs on parsers that hold a verification key

DefaultJwtParser.parse(String) ran signature verification only when the
compact token carried a signature segment. A token with an empty
signature segment, such as "header.payload." or an alg:none header with a
trailing dot, skipped verification. The parser then returned its claims
as a plain Jwt even when a Key, key bytes or a SigningKeyResolver was
configured (CWE-347). parse(String, JwtHandler), parseClaimsJwt and
parsePlaintextJwt inherited the problem.

parse(String) now throws UnsupportedJwtException for an unsigned token
when the parser holds any verification material. The check runs before
the resolver, claim validation, Jwt construction and any JwtHandler
callback, and it does not read the token's alg header. Parsers without
verification material and signed-token verification are unchanged.

Adds UnsignedJwtWithVerificationKeyTest.

Cgp-Finding: CGP-qfvj-qrwj-6c8w
